{"id":"whistleblower-trend","title":"Whistleblower reports: how many come in and what happens to them","tier":"OFFICIAL","question":"Are more people reporting wrongdoing in City government, and how often does a report end in action?","finding":"The Controller's program received 817 reports in FY2026, up from 732 in FY2022. It investigated and closed 422; 115 (27%) led a department or contractor to act, the lowest share in the 5 reports. Of the 124 actions that followed, 74 were policy or procedure changes and 38 were personnel actions still pending; 1 employee was terminated, 0 suspended, and no repayment was recorded.","how":"Read from the text of the five annual reports (fiscal 2022 to 2026): the key-statistics sentences and the \"report outcomes\" table. Each row links to its report.","limits":"A report is an allegation by anyone, most of them anonymous; many concern management decisions and not fraud. A personnel action still pending at year end may later become a suspension or termination that the next report does not trace back. The fiscal 2022 report has no repayment row.","columns":[{"k":"year","t":"Fiscal year","type":"text"},{"k":"received","t":"Reports received","type":"int"},{"k":"closed","t":"Closed","type":"int"},{"k":"investigated","t":"Investigated and closed","type":"int"},{"k":"ledToAction","t":"Led to action","type":"int"},{"k":"actionShare","t":"Share of investigations","type":"pct"},{"k":"terminated","t":"Employees terminated","type":"int"},{"k":"suspended","t":"Suspended","type":"int"},{"k":"restitution","t":"Repayments","type":"int"},{"k":"policyChanges","t":"Policy changes","type":"int"},{"k":"pending","t":"Personnel actions pending","type":"int"},{"k":"anonymousShare","t":"Filed anonymously","type":"pct"},{"k":"openAtYearEnd","t":"Open at year end","type":"int"},{"k":"link","t":"Report","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"year":"FY2022","received":732,"closed":703,"investigated":299,"ledToAction":92,"openAtYearEnd":82,"actionShare":0.308,"anonymousSha